Tftp-proxy is a proxy for the Trivial File Transfer Protocol. TFTP
connections on port 69 are redirected into the proxy via pf(4), after
which the proxy connects to the server on behalf of the client.

The proxy allows TFTP data connections to pass by registering dynamic
pf(4) anchors. The BSD tftp-proxy binary is already part of the base
system at /usr/libexec/tftp-proxy and is activated via inetd(8).

This plugin provides an OPNsense GUI and automatic pf anchor injection.

WWW: https://man.freebsd.org/cgi/man.cgi?tftp-proxy
